# `choose:` - subjectless cond-form (Minimal Orion: "match, den enda förgreningen").
#
# `choose:` with no scrutinee is a condition chain - the first true arm wins,
# `else:` is the catch-all. It replaces `if / else if / else`. Desugars to a
# right-nested if/else at parse time, so eval and typeck are untouched.
#
# Arms must be indented deeper than the `choose` keyword (same rule as a
# scrutinee `choose`).
#
# Run (lodge-orion interp):  orion run match_cond.or main   → expects 1

define main() -> number:
    score = 120
    choose:
        score > 100: 1     # first true arm wins  → 1
        score > 50:  2
        else:        0
